Third-party components:

The Rust crates built into the program are listed, each with its license, in THIRD-PARTY.md. All are under
permissive terms (MIT, Apache 2.0, BSD, Zlib, Unicode); where a crate offers a choice, the MIT or Apache 2.0
terms are used.

The Word 97-2003 reader follows Microsoft's published [MS-DOC] file format specification.

The PDF text and page drawing code adapts PrismQDA's PDF importer and page viewer (Apache License 2.0, same author).
Text recognition calls the recogniser built into Windows; no recognition engine is bundled.

The 31 interface icons in assets/icons that the icon brief (design/icons) marks as reused are copied unchanged from
PrismQDA's icon set (Apache License 2.0, same author).
